//
// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING:
// France is legally clear but deliberately restrictive, not a grey area
// like Spain and not permissive like Ireland/Denmark. Since the loi
// confortant le respect des principes de la République (August 2021,
// in full effect for new cases from September 2022), home education
// (instruction en famille / IEF) requires PRIOR AUTHORIZATION from the
// local education authority (DASEN), not just notification. Authorization
// is granted only on four narrow grounds: the child's health, intensive
// sport/artistic training, family travel/itinerant lifestyle, or a
// specific documented situation (e.g. genuine distance from any school).
// "We prefer an international curriculum" is explicitly NOT a valid
// ground, and advocacy groups report meaningfully high rejection rates
// even for previously well-regarded homeschool families.
//
// Do NOT write copy implying Smartious helps a family obtain IEF
// authorization on curriculum-preference grounds — that would be
// misleading. The honest, realistic positioning used throughout this
// file is: (1) families who already qualify on one of the four legal
// grounds (itinerant/diplomatic postings are a genuinely relevant
// segment given Strasbourg's EU institutions), or, far more commonly,
// (2) families who remain enrolled at a registered French or
// international school and use Smartious as supplementary/dual-track
// curriculum support — the same honest "administrative dual enrolment"
// pattern already used for Spain.
